>> B2: Describe how file descriptors are associated with open files.
>> Are file descriptors unique within the entire OS or just within a
>> single process?

Each process will own a list of fd_entry records. open() will create
a file handle and assign a descriptor starting at two. Numbers are local
to the process; zero and one are reserved for keyboard and console I/O.

Children will start with empty lists. Each open gets its own handle and
offset, even for the same file. close() will remove the entry, close the
handle, and free the node. Exit will close all remaining entries.

If entry allocation fails, close the new handle and return -1. Reject
next_fd values above INT_MAX before converting to int.

